# Our own sources can be normalised normally.
*.js       text
*.json     text
*.md       text
*.bat      text eol=crlf
.gitignore text

# Archived vendor files must round-trip through git byte-identically. Without
# this, git's CRLF normalisation would rewrite the mirrored bundles on checkout
# and a fresh clone would no longer match what was actually downloaded from
# qmk.top -- which defeats the point of keeping the .orig files.
#
# These come LAST on purpose: for a given attribute the last matching pattern
# wins, so listing them after "*.js text" is what keeps site/**/*.js binary.
site/**        -text
drivers/**     -text
build/**       -text
bundled-cache/**/*.json -text
